From b92d923177c0e8ec74d3f622b1e5a15ca4801b00 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nguyenyou <tunt081295@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 18:10:03 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(rust-js): serde_path_to_error says where in the value a
 read failed, as native serde_path_to_error does

serde_path_to_error joins the catalog of crates rust-js reads as rustc
builds them, qualified at 0.1.20 (ADR 1188). Its `deserialize` of
`serde_json::Deserializer::from_str(text)`'s reader is `$jsonPathRead`:
the runtime's reader keeping where in the value it is, by the crate's own
rules, and an error copying that place as it's made. A missing field is
at its struct, `customer: missing field `email``; an item at its index,
`items[1].qty`; a key's value at its text, an integer's digits, a bool's
word; a variant's content at its name; a key not yet read `?`; none for an
`Option`, a newtype, or a flattened or internally tagged variant's content.
Its `Error` is `{ path, original }`, shown as the crate shows it, plain,
`{:#?}`, `{:x?}`, a piece at a time into a writer, and as a `dyn Error`;
declared `@rust-js/std`'s opaque `JsonPathError` and `JsonPath`. A type's
own `deserialize` of the reader works too. A plain `serde_json::from_str`
keeps no place: each step one `undefined` test, its JS unchanged.

serde_json's reader's other methods stay refused (#1626), and so does the
crate's own `Track`, `Path::iter`, and a read of anything but serde_json's
reader of text. The struct reader asks its key for its field, `field()`,
so `deny_unknown_fields`' error is at the key.

Tests: test/serde-path.test.ts, against native serde_path_to_error;
22 mutations, each caught. Found by coming-from-zod's chapter 5.

Fixes #2379
Refs #1626

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01YLAVwjpnNqK2VBniftmdWk
